// A `comptime` parameter read as a VALUE inside a template that nothing instantiates. The
// uninstantiated-template probe walks these bodies with the parameter deliberately unbound (a probe has no
// argument to bind), so `N` is the one name that may legitimately reach the identifier arm with nothing
// binding it — the arm must DEFER it (counted, like every other probe residual), never report it as
// unresolved. Both halves of the probe are pinned: a generic function and a generic type.
fn int32 scaled<T>(T x) comptime(int32 N) { return N + 1; }
type value Buf<T> comptime(int32 N) {
    T v;
    public ctor of(T v) { this.v = v; }
    public fn int32 cap() { return N; }
}
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
